# Managed by league repo -- do not edit deployed copy
# Source: league/server/crontab-main/league-backups.cron
# Deploy: yarn load:crontab:main  (scope league-main -> league:~/crontab/league-backups.cron)
#
# League production Postgres backups — three year-round pipelines, plus one
# derived artifact that is not a backup at all.
#
#   full    — whole-DB pg_dump -Fd -j directory dump (ephemeral prop-pairing DATA
#             excluded via --exclude-table-data), Tue + Fri. The restorability
#             backbone; base-storage routes it to database-dumps/league-production/.
#   user    — small, irreplaceable, fast-changing slice (plain-SQL .tar.gz): a
#             dated daily time-series (7-day on-VPS window) plus a 15-min checkpoint
#             (latest overwritten in place) for ≤15-min on-prem RPO.
#   globals — pg_dumpall --globals-only, sops/age-encrypted. The roles and their
#             SCRAM verifiers, which pg_dump structurally cannot carry.
#
#   dev fixture — a SCRUBBED projection of the user slice, derived daily. Not a
#             backup, not restorable, and the only artifact a dev machine may pull.
#
# No season gate, no table-subset jobs — every table has a ≤3-4-day whole-DB copy
# year-round. The full's Tue+Fri schedule has a 4-day Fri→Tue gap, which would
# false-fire against a flat 3-day staleness default, so the full's line reports
# under a scheduled-command carrier entity via JOB_SCHEDULE_ENTITY_URI, whose
# staleness_window_seconds (5 days) tolerates the gap.
# The user dumps stay cron:* sources (daily / 15-min cadence < the 3-day default).
#
# Two corrections to what this comment used to claim (2026-07-29):
#   - "the oracle ignores JOB_SCHEDULE for cron:* sources" is no longer true in
#     general: check-stale-runs computes a next-expected-fire from the cadence
#     `base run report --schedule` puts on the ledger row. It is still true in
#     EFFECT on this host, for a different reason -- league's base CLI is the
#     compiled 2026.07.05 build with no --schedule flag, so job-wrapper.sh's
#     degrade path strips the cadence and every cron:league:* row has schedule
#     NULL. Do not rely on JOB_SCHEDULE here until that CLI is upgraded.
#   - The carrier below is NOT currently being monitored. league-backup-full.md
#     carries `enabled: false` (correct: no dispatcher should fire it, the line
#     below does), but check-stale-runs treats enabled:false as a deliberate
#     stand-down and skips the source before any staleness math. So its 5-day
#     window is inert. The backup itself is still covered by the content-freshness
#     checks on base-storage; it is the runs-layer redundancy that is missing.
#
# Offset minute marks (3-48/15, 6-56/10, 1-56/5, ...) are DELIBERATE, not typos
# for the round form. Every recurring cadence used to land on :00 and :30, which
# put 22 jobs in one minute at midnight and 11 at 04:30. Spreading them across
# residues drops the year's peak to 6. Before restoring any of these to */N,
# re-run the peak check -- one "tidy" undoes the whole spread.

# Full whole-DB dump (directory format, parallel) — Tuesday + Friday 08:00 UTC (off-peak)
0 8 * * 2,5 JOB_SCHEDULE_ENTITY_URI=user:scheduled-command/league/league-backup-full.md job-wrapper.sh league-backup-full /bin/bash /root/league/scripts/postgres-backup.sh -f >> /var/log/league/league-postgres-backup.log 2>&1

# User dump — daily time-series (dated, 7-day window) at 00:00 UTC
0 0 * * * job-wrapper.sh league-backup-user-timeseries /bin/bash /root/league/scripts/postgres-backup.sh >> /var/log/league/league-postgres-backup.log 2>&1

# User dump — 15-minute checkpoint (latest overwritten in place) year-round
3-48/15 * * * * job-wrapper.sh league-backup-user-checkpoint /bin/bash /root/league/scripts/postgres-backup.sh -n checkpoint >> /var/log/league/league-postgres-backup.log 2>&1

# Scrubbed dev fixture — daily 00:23 UTC, latest overwritten in place.
#
# This is NOT a backup and has no recovery value: it is the only artifact a dev
# machine is allowed to pull. The user dump above stays complete and unscrubbed
# because it is the DR artifact for the irreplaceable slice — a scrubbed backup
# cannot restore the users, invite codes, webhooks, wagers or vendor config it
# redacted. So the scrub happens on the path to DEV, not on the path to the
# backup, and it happens here, on the host that already holds the plaintext.
#
# The scrub is an explicit emitted-column projection over every column of every
# dumped table (scripts/dev-fixture-projection.json); a column present in the
# database but absent from the spec ABORTS the run with no artifact written.
# That is what makes the schedule load-bearing rather than a convenience: a
# migration that adds a column turns this job red the next morning instead of
# quietly emitting an unadjudicated field. Running it by hand would defer that
# alarm until someone remembered to pull a fixture.
#
# No time series and no retention prune: a fixture has no recovery value, so
# depth is pure carrying cost. The deriver writes to a temp path and renames, so
# the hourly base-storage pull can never read a half-written artifact — the same
# atomicity the checkpoint above needed after the 2026-08-03 truncation.
#
# Minute 23 collides with nothing: the */15 checkpoint fires at :00/:15/:30/:45
# and league-imports.cron's */10 poll at :00/:10/:20/:30/:40/:50.
23 0 * * * job-wrapper.sh league-derive-dev-fixture /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/derive-dev-fixture.mjs --name latest >> /var/log/league/league-postgres-backup.log 2>&1

# Cluster globals — roles, their passwords, their per-role settings, their grants.
# Daily, sops/age-encrypted, latest overwritten in place.
#
# `pg_dump` is per-DATABASE, so neither pipeline above carries pg_authid or
# pg_db_role_setting: until 2026-08-04 a rebuild restored all 279 tables and then
# could not connect, because league_writer and league_reader did not exist. The
# artifact is ENCRYPTED (it holds every login role's SCRAM verifier) to the
# narrow {league, macbook2025} recipient set in /root/league/.sops.yaml, so
# base-storage stores it and cannot read it.
#
# Daily rather than at the full's Tue/Fri cadence: the dump is a sub-second read
# of three small catalogs, and role state changes on its own schedule (a password
# rotation or an ALTER ROLE SET lands on whatever day it lands). A daily source
# also sits under check-stale-runs' flat 3-day default, so it needs no
# scheduled-command carrier entity — unlike the full above, whose 4-day Fri->Tue
# gap did.
#
# Minute 37 is chosen to collide with nothing: the */15 checkpoint above fires at
# :00/:15/:30/:45 and league-imports.cron's */10 draft-notifications poll at
# :00/:10/:20/:30/:40/:50. 09:xx UTC keeps it clear of the 08:00 full, which runs
# for minutes.
37 9 * * * job-wrapper.sh league-backup-globals /bin/bash /root/league/scripts/postgres-globals-backup.sh >> /var/log/league/league-postgres-backup.log 2>&1
